.so fork.tmac
.PP
.pt_jd_Node
.RS 4
.TP
.I parent
.TQ
.I nextSibling
.TQ
.I firstChild
.TQ
.I prevSibling
.TQ
.I lastChild
are pointers to related nodes.
The first four follow HTML/CSS conventions of organization,
with children of a node accessed through the first child and
through the siblings of the first child.
.IP
The order of the related nodes copies the order of sides of a CSS page,
top, right, bottom, and left.
.IP
.I lastChild
is used for appending a new child of a node to avoid having to
walk through all children to find the last.
.TP
.I type
indicates what type of data to which the
.I payload
member points.
.IP
See the
.B TYPES
section below to find the
.B jd_Type
enumeration.
.TP
.I payload
is non-typed pointer meant to be cast to the proper type as
directed by the
.I type
member.
.TP
.I name
points to a
.B char*
if a name is needed for the node.  Child nodes of an object
must have names.
.RE
